This product includes model weights derived from knowledgator/gliclass-multilang-edge
(https://huggingface.co/knowledgator/gliclass-multilang-edge), licensed under the
Apache License 2.0, Copyright Knowledgator. Modifications: vocabulary trimmed to 32,768
tokens (en/it/es/de/fr), fine-tuning on MASSIVE train utterances (49 intents) and, for the
phase 2 models such as edge32k-ft6, on the yes/no, agent-action and breadth data listed
below; an 8-layer student distilled from a phase 1 model; ONNX export, weight-only and dynamic
int8 quantization.

Baseline measurements use convaiinnovations/laya-multilingual (Apache License 2.0,
Copyright Convai Innovations). Its weights are not part of the git repository; the ONNX
conversions used as baselines are distributed only as release files, under the original
Apache License 2.0 with this attribution.

Benchmark data in bench/data/ is derived from MASSIVE (Amazon, CC BY 4.0,
https://github.com/alexa/massive), obtained via mteb/amazon_massive_intent. Option
descriptions and yes/no questions were added by the Skejja project.

The vocabulary selection used a sample of Wikipedia sentences (CC BY-SA 4.0) only to
count token frequencies; no Wikipedia text is redistributed.

Phase 2 yes/no (Noul) data in bench/data/ext/ and bench/data/*_ext.jsonl is derived from:
- CLINC150 (Larson et al., 2019; https://github.com/clinc/oos-eval), CC BY 3.0, obtained via
  clinc/clinc_oos on Hugging Face;
- BANKING77 (Casanueva et al., 2020; https://github.com/PolyAI-LDN/task-specific-datasets),
  CC BY 4.0;
- MINDS-14 (Gerz et al., 2021; https://huggingface.co/datasets/PolyAI/minds14), CC BY 4.0
  (text transcriptions only).
Changes: intents related to the MASSIVE held-out scenarios removed, intent descriptions and
yes/no questions added by the Skejja project, part of the English sentences machine-translated
into Italian, Spanish, German and French with OPUS-MT models (Helsinki-NLP/opus-mt-en-it,
-en-es, -en-fr: Apache License 2.0; -en-de: CC BY 4.0).

Agent-action yes/no data in bench/data/agent/ is derived from tldr-pages
(https://github.com/tldr-pages/tldr, revision b9650ebb236ac9ca2ce11a5f1f15d72794f36c4a),
CC BY 4.0, Copyright the tldr-pages team and contributors. Changes: example commands and their
descriptions (English, Italian, Spanish, German, French) extracted, placeholders rendered, and
yes/no property labels added by rule-based heuristics of the Skejja project.

Phase 2 breadth data in bench/data/broad/ (used to train edge32k-ft6) contains:
- texts sampled from FineWeb-2 and FineWeb (HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-2, HuggingFaceFW/fineweb),
  ODC-By 1.0, derived from Common Crawl and subject to the Common Crawl Terms of Use;
- texts sampled from the Aya Dataset (CohereLabs/aya_dataset), Apache License 2.0, Copyright
  Cohere For AI and the Aya contributors;
- texts sampled from MFAQ (clips/mfaq), CC0 1.0;
- synthetic texts (synth_texts.jsonl, requests_synth.jsonl.gz) generated by Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B,
  and soft labels for all breadth requests produced by the same model (labels_*.jsonl*).
  Qwen3.5-9B is licensed under the Apache License 2.0, Copyright Alibaba Cloud (Qwen team).
Changes: texts selected per language, filtered by length and share of letters, and deduplicated
against texts already used by the project; task families, questions and option descriptions
written by the Skejja project; labels are teacher-model probabilities, not human annotations.
Training splits of SST-2, AG News, Emotion and SMS Spam were used only to measure the teacher
model; they are not redistributed and were not used to train Skejja.
